# Bit-correctness: block-ILUT saddle preconditioner with a PARTIAL fix group.
#
# This is the case that would have caught the segfault. It is the metal_ilu deck with ONE change
# -- `fix beq all` -> `fix beq sub`, so the single type-1 molecule atom sits OUTSIDE the qeq group.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: compute_H and compute_X fill H/X firstnbr/numnbrs only for group rows, and
# allocate_matrix uses memory->create (malloc, not calloc). Before the fix, ilu_build() walked those
# arrays for EVERY local atom, so a non-group atom sent it into uninitialised heap -- SIGSEGV, or on
# a lucky heap a silently polluted factor. Every existing ILU deck used group == all, so the whole
# suite was blind to it; the gated-Drude melt (group = CORES, 1680 shells outside) is what exposed it.
#
# Pre-fix this deck segfaults. Post-fix it must produce finite, locked charges.
units           metal
atom_style      full
boundary        f f f
lattice         sc 1.5
region          box block -20 20 -20 20 -5 30 units box
create_box      2 box
region          slab block -3 3 -3 3 -0.1 0.1 units box
create_atoms    2 region slab
create_atoms    1 single 0.0 0.0 2.0 units box
mass            * 12.0
group           sub  type 2
group           mol  type 1
set             group sub mol 2
set             group mol mol 1
set             group all charge 0.0
pair_style      zero 14.0
pair_coeff      * *
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check no
fix             beq sub qeq/sam 1 0.0 14.0 1.0e-10 iface_metal.param
fix_modify      beq precond ilu
compute         cq all property/atom q
compute         qmol mol reduce sum c_cq
variable        qm equal c_qmol
run             0
write_dump      all custom charges.dump id type q modify sort id format line "%d %d %.12g"
print           "${qm}" file pe.txt screen no
write_dump      all custom charges.dump id type q modify sort id format line "%d %d %.12g"
